Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a constant-radius blend whose ball would lie beyond a support's
centre of curvature along the guide is walked with its sections in the
guide's normal plane, as OCCT walks every one (mitcad#1977).

Patch 0075 made the walked constant-radius blend a true rolling ball: its
centre at the radius along both surfaces' unit normals. That ball exists
only where it fits a support from the side of its centre. A rim rounded
with a ball larger than the roundings of the corners it runs round (a
cast part's top edge rounded with 6.096 round drafted corners rounded with
3.048) asks, round each corner, for a ball whose centre at the radius from
the corner's rounding, towards its axis, lies beyond that axis: the
equations then hold for a ball that holds the rounding's section, and the
sections fold back. OCCT's walk failed there (a walking failure, the
whole chain of 16 edges one faulty contour), and just above the corners'
radius it built an invalid result; before 0075, with the sections in the
guide's normal plane, the same roundings built, valid, as the file the
case comes from stores them (its volume within 2e-6).

- BlendFunc_ConstRad::BallBeyondSupport (new, static): a cylinder, cone,
  sphere or torus that curves along the guide (its normal curvature in the
  guide's direction at the guide's middle, where the guide lies on it)
  towards the ball's centre with a radius of curvature smaller than the
  ball's by more than 1e-6. A ball of the support's own radius (1520's
  tubes) is not beyond it, nor is one that rolls along a direction in which
  the support curves less (a foot rounding of 2 along a corner torus whose
  tube is 1.5, round the torus's axis: patch 0460's case in
  test_fillet_corners stays the rolling ball).
- BlendFunc_ConstRad::Set(Radius, Choix) and BlendFunc_ConstRadInv's take
  the guide's normal plane where either support has the ball beyond it;
  ComputeValues, IsSolution, Tangent and the four Sections of
  BlendFunc_ConstRad, and Value and Values of BlendFunc_ConstRadInv, are
  then OCCT 8.0.1's own (BlendFunc_ConstRad_GuidePlane.cxx, the functions
  renamed; StillSection gives none). The caches are cleared when the mode
  changes. BlendFunc_ConstRadInv's derivatives go through Values, whose
  derivative of the guide's plane is the right one (0075's note).

Elsewhere nothing changes: a blend whose ball fits both supports is the
rolling ball of 0075 and its successors.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_ball_beyond_support.cpp, a block drafted
by 2.5 degrees, its corners rounded with 3, its top's rim rounded with 4,
6 and 8 (without the patch 6 failed and 4 was invalid) and on both sides
of the corners' radius (2.985 to 3.015: 3.005 and 3.015 were invalid), by
OCCT's fillet alone.

Upstream: with 0075 (OCCT walks in the guide's normal plane everywhere).

